#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:40
msgid "NARMA"
msgstr "NARMA"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:42
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The Nonlinear Auto-Regressive Moving Average "
"(:class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.narma.NARMA`) benchmark is a system-"
"identification task. A random input stream :math:`u(t) \\sim "
"\\mathcal{U}(0, 0.5)` drives an order-:math:`n` nonlinear recurrence "
"whose output :math:`y(t)` must be predicted from :math:`u`:"
msgstr ""
"El punto de referencia de media móvil autorregresiva no lineal "
"(:class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.narma.NARMA`) es una tarea de "
"identificación de sistemas. Un flujo de entrada aleatorio :math:`u(t) "
"\\sim \\mathcal{U}(0, 0.5)` excita una recurrencia no lineal de orden "
":math:`n` cuya salida :math:`y(t)` debe predecirse a partir de :math:`u`:"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:46
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"y(t+1) = \\alpha\\, y(t)\n"
"         + \\beta\\, y(t) \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} y(t-i)\n"
"         + \\gamma\\, u(t-n+1)\\, u(t)\n"
"         + \\delta."
msgstr ""
"y(t+1) = \\alpha\\, y(t)\n         + \\beta\\, y(t) \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} "
"y(t-i)\n         + \\gamma\\, u(t-n+1)\\, u(t)\n         + \\delta."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:53
msgid ""
"The default coefficients :math:`(\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma, \\delta) = "
"(0.3, 0.05, 1.5, 0.1)` correspond to the ubiquitous ``NARMA10`` task "
"(``order=10``). Unlike the other generators, ``inputs`` are the random "
"drive :math:`u` and ``targets`` are the system response :math:`y`; both "
"are shaped ``(npoints, 1)``. Because the drive is random, a ``seed`` can "
"be specified to ensure reproducibility."
msgstr ""
"Los coeficientes por defecto :math:`(\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma, \\delta) = "
"(0.3, 0.05, 1.5, 0.1)` corresponden a la omnipresente tarea ``NARMA10`` "
"(``order=10``). A diferencia de los demás generadores, ``inputs`` es la "
"excitación aleatoria :math:`u` y ``targets`` es la respuesta del sistema "
":math:`y`; ambos tienen forma ``(npoints, 1)``. Como la excitación es "
"aleatoria, se puede especificar una ``seed`` para garantizar la "
"reproducibilidad."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:65
msgid "MackeyGlass"
msgstr "MackeyGlass"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:67
msgid ""
"The :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.mackey_glass.MackeyGlass` system is a "
"nonlinear delay differential equation that produces a chaotic attractor:"
msgstr ""
"El sistema :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.mackey_glass.MackeyGlass` es una "
"ecuación diferencial con retardo no lineal que produce un atractor "
"caótico:"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:70
msgid ""
"\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\beta\\, \\frac{x(t - \\tau)}{1 + x(t - \\tau)^{n}}\n"
"                - \\gamma\\, x(t)."
msgstr ""
"\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\beta\\, \\frac{x(t - \\tau)}{1 + x(t - \\tau)^{n}}\n   "
"             - \\gamma\\, x(t)."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:75
msgid ""
"With the standard parameters :math:`\\beta = 0.2`, :math:`\\gamma = 0.1`,"
" :math:`n = 10`, the behaviour is set by the delay :math:`\\tau`: the "
"series is periodic for small :math:`\\tau`, mildly chaotic at "
":math:`\\tau = 17`, and increasingly chaotic beyond. The equation is "
"integrated with a fixed-step RK4 scheme at resolution ``dt`` and sub-"
"sampled every ``sample_every`` steps."
msgstr ""
"Con los parámetros estándar :math:`\\beta = 0.2`, :math:`\\gamma = 0.1`, "
":math:`n = 10`, el comportamiento lo fija el retardo :math:`\\tau`: la "
"serie es periódica para :math:`\\tau` pequeños, ligeramente caótica en "
":math:`\\tau = 17` y cada vez más caótica más allá. La ecuación se "
"integra con un esquema RK4 de paso fijo con resolución ``dt`` y se "
"submuestrea cada ``sample_every`` pasos."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:88
msgid "Lorenz"
msgstr "Lorenz"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:90
msgid ""
"The :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.lorenz.Lorenz` attractor is a three-"
"dimensional chaotic dynamical system:"
msgstr ""
"El atractor :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.lorenz.Lorenz` es un sistema "
"dinámico caótico tridimensional:"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:92
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\dot{x} = \\sigma (y - x), \\quad\n"
"\\dot{y} = x (\\rho - z) - y, \\quad\n"
"\\dot{z} = x y - \\beta z."
msgstr ""
"\\dot{x} = \\sigma (y - x), \\quad\n\\dot{y} = x (\\rho - z) - y, "
"\\quad\n\\dot{z} = x y - \\beta z."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:98
msgid ""
"The trajectory is integrated with RK4 and sub-sampled, yielding a "
"``horizon``-step-ahead prediction task over the three-dimensional state, "
"so ``inputs`` and ``targets`` are both shaped ``(npoints, 3)``."
msgstr ""
"La trayectoria se integra con RK4 y se submuestrea, lo que da lugar a una "
"tarea de predicción de ``horizon`` pasos por delante sobre el estado "
"tridimensional, por lo que ``inputs`` y ``targets`` tienen ambos forma "
"``(npoints, 3)``."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:109
msgid "SantaFeLaser"
msgstr "SantaFeLaser"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:111
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The original *Santa Fe Time Series Competition* Data Set A is a recording"
" of the chaotic intensity pulsations of a far-infrared "
":math:`\\mathrm{NH_3}` laser. Rather than shipping the recording, "
":class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.santa_fe_laser.SantaFeLaser` reproduces the "
"same qualitative dynamics from first principles using the single-mode "
"**Lorenz--Haken** laser equations:"
msgstr ""
"El conjunto de datos A original de la *Santa Fe Time Series Competition* "
"es una grabación de las pulsaciones caóticas de intensidad de un láser de "
":math:`\\mathrm{NH_3}` de infrarrojo lejano. En lugar de distribuir la "
"grabación, :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.santa_fe_laser.SantaFeLaser` "
"reproduce la misma dinámica cualitativa desde primeros principios "
"mediante las ecuaciones de láser **Lorenz--Haken** de un solo modo:"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:116
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\dot{E} = \\sigma (P - E), \\quad\n"
"\\dot{P} = E (\\rho - N) - P, \\quad\n"
"\\dot{N} = E P - \\beta N,"
msgstr ""
"\\dot{E} = \\sigma (P - E), \\quad\n\\dot{P} = E (\\rho - N) - P, "
"\\quad\n\\dot{N} = E P - \\beta N,"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:122
msgid ""
"where :math:`E` is the field amplitude, :math:`P` the polarization and "
":math:`N` the population inversion. The measured quantity is the laser "
"**intensity** :math:`I \\propto E^2`, which is non-negative and "
"reproduces the behaviour of the Santa Fe recording. Both ``inputs`` and "
"``targets`` are shaped ``(npoints, 1)``."
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`E` es la amplitud del campo, :math:`P` la polarización y "
":math:`N` la inversión de población. La magnitud medida es la "
"**intensidad** del láser :math:`I \\propto E^2`, que es no negativa y "
"reproduce el comportamiento de la grabación de Santa Fe. Tanto ``inputs`` "
"como ``targets`` tienen forma ``(npoints, 1)``."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:134
msgid "HenonMap"
msgstr "HenonMap"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:136
msgid ""
"The :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.henon.HenonMap` is a two-dimensional "
"discrete chaotic system:"
msgstr ""
"El :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.henon.HenonMap` es un sistema caótico "
"discreto bidimensional:"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:138
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"x_{n+1} = 1 - a\\, x_n^2 + y_n, \\qquad\n"
"y_{n+1} = b\\, x_n,"
msgstr ""
"x_{n+1} = 1 - a\\, x_n^2 + y_n, \\qquad\ny_{n+1} = b\\, x_n,"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:143
msgid ""
"which is chaotic for the parameters :math:`a = 1.4`, :math:`b = 0.3`. "
":meth:`generate` returns a ``horizon``-step-ahead prediction task over "
"the two-dimensional state, so ``inputs`` and ``targets`` are both shaped "
"``(npoints, 2)``."
msgstr ""
"que es caótico para los parámetros :math:`a = 1.4`, :math:`b = 0.3`. "
":meth:`generate` devuelve una tarea de predicción de ``horizon`` pasos "
"por delante sobre el estado bidimensional, por lo que ``inputs`` y "
"``targets`` tienen ambos forma ``(npoints, 2)``."

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:154
msgid "LogisticMap"
msgstr "LogisticMap"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:156
msgid ""
"The :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.logistic_map.LogisticMap` is a simple "
"one-dimensional chaotic system:"
msgstr ""
"El :class:`~qilisdk.ml.datasets.logistic_map.LogisticMap` es un sistema "
"caótico unidimensional sencillo:"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:158
#, python-brace-format
msgid "x_{n+1} = r\\, x_n (1 - x_n),"
msgstr "x_{n+1} = r\\, x_n (1 - x_n),"

#: ../../modules/ml/ml_datasets.rst:162
msgid ""
"which becomes chaotic as the growth rate :math:`r` approaches 4 (the "
"default :math:`r = 3.9` sits well inside the chaotic regime). "
":meth:`generate` returns a ``horizon``-step-ahead prediction task, so "
"``inputs`` and ``targets`` are shaped ``(npoints, 1)``."
msgstr ""
"que se vuelve caótico a medida que la tasa de crecimiento :math:`r` se "
"acerca a 4 (el valor por defecto :math:`r = 3.9` se sitúa bien dentro del "
"régimen caótico). :meth:`generate` devuelve una tarea de predicción de "
"``horizon`` pasos por delante, por lo que ``inputs`` y ``targets`` tienen "
"forma ``(npoints, 1)``."

